[{:db/id "q-119760/selection/1df9f8f6a1e4ed264e585db71466b0b88df786fd85a8973741a5587a9bb5382e" :answer/id #uuid "5c6eff06-7cac-5acf-b119-a20deb81dfcd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$5.5$ million years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760/selection/deba1d66d954a36184e81f5bde9ee19651d9583ccb818f537e21cf1a0ff81da1" :answer/id #uuid "5f2bd982-8568-5506-af60-fb5e30ecf8e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$20.0$ million years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760/selection/2f5d0c99d05f9c01d1b8fa6a4fb11765be108a10312b116fb81b9649163778bf" :answer/id #uuid "179d1858-7355-5512-9f12-5dd4b3479f0e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$12.8$ million years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760/selection/c6e08aff0b836b0817e35b83e4f93cd1f436d0bd01dbf2d67e56aa19b8336486" :answer/id #uuid "34f3f7bf-af4a-5da8-be20-569298142498" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$8.0$ million years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760/selection/acd4e2b1b9a52e756e58cbbeecfd164267401bcbe11854143a6dcf6c8eaf9f80" :answer/id #uuid "7f02c6ed-c5f2-59ef-9edb-9bc3a640f332" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3.7$ million years" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8edc12f9-903f-5a04-8b23-34bdcb090a24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-119760/selection/acd4e2b1b9a52e756e58cbbeecfd164267401bcbe11854143a6dcf6c8eaf9f80" :answer-field/choices ["q-119760/selection/1df9f8f6a1e4ed264e585db71466b0b88df786fd85a8973741a5587a9bb5382e" "q-119760/selection/deba1d66d954a36184e81f5bde9ee19651d9583ccb818f537e21cf1a0ff81da1" "q-119760/selection/2f5d0c99d05f9c01d1b8fa6a4fb11765be108a10312b116fb81b9649163778bf" "q-119760/selection/c6e08aff0b836b0817e35b83e4f93cd1f436d0bd01dbf2d67e56aa19b8336486" "q-119760/selection/acd4e2b1b9a52e756e58cbbeecfd164267401bcbe11854143a6dcf6c8eaf9f80"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-119760" :question/id #uuid "942dc377-e586-5f6a-b84b-ba62f5470c32" :question/math-academy-id "q-119760" :question/problem "The mass $M(t),$ in micrograms, of a sample of manganese-53 is given by\n\n$$\nM(t)=17{e}^{-0.187t},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in millions of years. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the half-life of manganese-53?" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $k=0.187.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1/2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{0.187} \\\\  & ≈3.7\\,\\text{million years}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-119760/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "589c680e-9f93-58e9-9dab-c34de98d7225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-119760"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-355590/field-1/8187114619eece79fc55b2e3c471451d09707ac94364ef88dab33c3668ae856b" :answer/id #uuid "d3fa9111-c3ec-5f63-9587-7130a525b58b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0403" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355590/field-1/fa2936f764d2276bb68faa99b141e16520d2aa5897d8a43f2ad94036321e1463" :answer/id #uuid "b1188e4d-3c45-5235-848f-b49d4a83c948" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0581" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-355590/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "12f92ae1-6312-53a4-9b2f-7e844073eaa0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-355590/field-1/8187114619eece79fc55b2e3c471451d09707ac94364ef88dab33c3668ae856b" :answer-field/choices ["q-355590/field-1/8187114619eece79fc55b2e3c471451d09707ac94364ef88dab33c3668ae856b" "q-355590/field-1/fa2936f764d2276bb68faa99b141e16520d2aa5897d8a43f2ad94036321e1463"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-355590" :question/id #uuid "5b92ee80-15ee-5d9a-b5d0-749a778570d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-355590" :question/problem "The mass $M(t),$ in micrograms, of a sample of neon-19 is given by\n\n$$\nM(t)=4.5{e}^{-kt},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in seconds. The half-life of neon-19 is $17.2\\,\\text{s}.$ Rounded to **three significant figures**, what is the value of $k?$\n\n$k≈$\n{{field-1}} ${\\text{s}}^{-1}$" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nSince we know that ${t}_{1/2}=17.2\\,\\text{s},$ we have\n\n$$\n17.2=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}\\,⇒\\,k=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{17.2}≈0.0403\\,{\\text{s}}^{-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-355590/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "589c680e-9f93-58e9-9dab-c34de98d7225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-355590"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection/92cae4fb2c9487a120e8c2150d9245b6d1e4f9347bb4f3c1bc236700c0d4efb8" :answer/id #uuid "8e147f5a-f20d-55c6-98ec-7813403870a5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$26.6$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection/8f43b9d758aa8fae0752429948dec964e1229f1caedb4c859d7d632f63ae0b18" :answer/id #uuid "225c6fe3-d979-5a79-ab39-fe1eac10fdf9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$25.2$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection/7bb42a3e0f40688f8862886a93746075799e12c7cdece668106df21376ebb99d" :answer/id #uuid "a5000016-075b-5afc-a3bf-4ffe1bef92d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27.4$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection/f3bda3b1d0382b3238e30c661dbc5ddbc153a8d2f9b2bff399634468d485376d" :answer/id #uuid "0a0a40ce-91b2-5703-8b92-73e73a4221d2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27.0$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection/5bbb012bcf117fad9d93f8acd880cd512510d3b66697c92f0e04f3975f6ca2ad" :answer/id #uuid "d8313d91-f16c-515b-b254-b4a486a6a738" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$27.8$ days" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0709e52b-f165-5efc-a44f-7a037e104f52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-118595/selection/f3bda3b1d0382b3238e30c661dbc5ddbc153a8d2f9b2bff399634468d485376d" :answer-field/choices ["q-118595/selection/92cae4fb2c9487a120e8c2150d9245b6d1e4f9347bb4f3c1bc236700c0d4efb8" "q-118595/selection/8f43b9d758aa8fae0752429948dec964e1229f1caedb4c859d7d632f63ae0b18" "q-118595/selection/7bb42a3e0f40688f8862886a93746075799e12c7cdece668106df21376ebb99d" "q-118595/selection/f3bda3b1d0382b3238e30c661dbc5ddbc153a8d2f9b2bff399634468d485376d" "q-118595/selection/5bbb012bcf117fad9d93f8acd880cd512510d3b66697c92f0e04f3975f6ca2ad"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-118595" :question/id #uuid "75995316-2591-577f-8d7d-d7868868827f" :question/math-academy-id "q-118595" :question/problem "The mass $M(t),$ in micrograms, of a sample of curium-240 is given by\n\n$$\nM(t)=8{e}^{-0.025\\,67t},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in days. Rounded to one decimal place, what is the half-life of curium-240?" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nWe're given that $k=0.025\\,67.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}_{1/2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{0.025\\,67} \\\\  & ≈27.0\\,\\text{days}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-118595/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "589c680e-9f93-58e9-9dab-c34de98d7225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-118595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection/de69cfe5ad39456e10f7be2f91a62bd382b917ed01b1d07a0025e0f4a91a8acf" :answer/id #uuid "8826e39b-7db0-58b4-9861-e3748ad80c85" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection/0de9eff32f0716c584bebd715cba47ba94b03a95c81e3c0d675b3a8952b2a50e" :answer/id #uuid "d0bad829-d886-5260-8ed9-461df5bc5c67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0157" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection/09c078054a1da2968224c26e26e7b021ceea91c8fbce49308b0e17887f844fec" :answer/id #uuid "84502056-cc8a-5e63-8f47-348a95e72219" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.433" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection/7632f4324280eed267bc049946a370a6be8281b41654c82cd967420faa0bb97a" :answer/id #uuid "077a7323-dead-5903-b9ca-ed61e69be9f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.153" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection/3e8a0a481ec9c89ad41d8273bb51e078dbc27afa6c9499dbe0f4a98a7ef6ce7c" :answer/id #uuid "11e399e2-75d8-5575-a351-235e17dc6eb6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.0561" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a4976827-8bc5-552f-b081-24f66917724e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-15588/selection/3e8a0a481ec9c89ad41d8273bb51e078dbc27afa6c9499dbe0f4a98a7ef6ce7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-15588/selection/de69cfe5ad39456e10f7be2f91a62bd382b917ed01b1d07a0025e0f4a91a8acf" "q-15588/selection/0de9eff32f0716c584bebd715cba47ba94b03a95c81e3c0d675b3a8952b2a50e" "q-15588/selection/09c078054a1da2968224c26e26e7b021ceea91c8fbce49308b0e17887f844fec" "q-15588/selection/7632f4324280eed267bc049946a370a6be8281b41654c82cd967420faa0bb97a" "q-15588/selection/3e8a0a481ec9c89ad41d8273bb51e078dbc27afa6c9499dbe0f4a98a7ef6ce7c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-15588" :question/id #uuid "0c54428c-f314-5348-b825-fad7c2d63d35" :question/math-academy-id "q-15588" :question/problem "The mass $M(t),$ in micrograms, of a sample of potassium-42 is given by\n\n$$\nM(t)=30{e}^{-kt},\n$$\n\nwhere $t$ is the time, in hours. The half-life of potassium-42 is $12.36\\,\\text{h}.$ Rounded to three significant figures, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "The mass $M(t)$ of a radioactive substance at time $t$ can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n{M}^{′}(t)=-kM(t),\\,M(0)={M}_{0}.\n$$\n\nThe general solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nM(t)={M}_{0}{e}^{-kt}.\n$$\n\nThe half-life ${t}_{1/2}$ is the time taken for the mass of the substance to reduce by one half and is given by\n\n$$\n{t}_{1/2}=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}.\n$$\n\nSince we know that ${t}_{1/2}=12.36\\,\\text{h}$ we have\n\n$$\n12.36=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{k}\\,⇒\\,k=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{12.36}≈0.0561\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-15588/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "589c680e-9f93-58e9-9dab-c34de98d7225"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-15588"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-118593/selection/7ec97e815dfea32